~ amador_intro
# Intro of the game
Amador: My head.. it [shake]hurts[/shake].
Amador: Wh... What am I doing here? Hold on, isn't this the [shake]basement?[/shake] 
??: [pulse]Look around, Amador[/pulse] 
=> END

~ amador_first_step
# This plays after trying to exit the basement without a key.
% Amador: The door's closed. I should find the key first.
% Amador: It's no use; the door's closed. Where was the key?
=> END

~ amador_first_chain_found_locker
# This plays after seeing the locker without the key.
% Amador: Hmm...maybe the key is inside the locker.
% Amador: ...wasn't the key in there?
=> END

~ amador_first_chain_found_first
# This plays after searching the box (First Number).
% Amador: There are 2 clocks inside.
% Amador: Two clocks...I cannot remember when did I put those in there.
=> END

~ amador_first_chain_found_second
# This plays after searching the bookshelf (Second Number).
The name of this book is [i]The Big Four[/i].
% Amador: I should read this sometime.
% Amador: My father brought it last year. I couldn't find time to read it yet.
=> END

~ amador_first_chain_found_last
# This plays after unveiling the painting (Third Number).
The painting shows both of your children. Lucas wears a cap with the number 9 on it.
% Amador: Maite painted it...I wonder where are they now.
% Amador: I love this painting. It's so [shake]beautiful[/shake].
=> END

~ amador_first_chain_open_locker
# This plays after opening the locker
% Amador: The key to the door; let's get out of here.
% Amador: Finally, the key in my hands. Let's open the door.
=> END

~ amador_tv
# TV machine
The TV turns on, letting out an annoying static noise.
...
Maite: [i]We should clean up the basement; it's a bit messy, after all.[/i]
...
...
Maite: [i]And the washimg machine... isn't it broken?? It surely belongs in the trash.[/i]
...
Maite: [i]The books do look interesting, though. We are keeping them.[/i]
=> END

~ amador_bookshelf
# Bookshelf
% Amador: There may be something here... in-between this pile of books.
% Amador: Can't see a thing here. Let's search deeper.

- Look inside => amador_first_chain_found_second
- Do nothing => END

~ amador_cute_box
# Cute box
% Amador: What a mess...let's see what's inside.
% Amador: Why did I leave this here? Maybe opening it will clear that up.

- Look inside => amador_first_chain_found_first
- Do nothing => END

~ amador_hidden_painting
# Painting
% Amador: Looks like a painting. It's so dusty...
% Amador: Wonder what's under this...let's see.
=> END

~ amador_opens_door
# This plays when opening the door with the key
[i]Amador opens the basement door.[/i]
=> END
